<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); (object == null && this.get(i) == null) || (object != null && object.equals(this.get(i)));</code>

However, the comment seems to imply a condition about the element at the index related to the newly added object. Given the context, it seems more appropriate to check the condition specifically for the newly added object:

<code>assert (object == null && this.get(this.size() - 1) == null) || (object != null && object.equals(this.get(this.size() - 1)));</code>

This ensures that the newly added object is correctly placed at the end of the set and matches the condition specified in the comment.
